---
import ToolPage from '../../../components/ToolPage.astro';
import TireSizeTechnicalVisual from '../../../components/TireSizeTechnicalVisual.astro';
import TireCodeExplainer from '../../../components/TireCodeExplainer.astro';
import { toolById } from '../../../seo/tool-registry';
const definition = toolById('tire-size-calculator');
---
<ToolPage {definition} alternates={[{ hreflang: 'en', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/tools/tire-size-calculator/' }, { hreflang: 'de', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/de/tools/reifengroesse-rechner/' }, { hreflang: 'es', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/es/tools/calculadora-tamano-neumaticos/' }, { hreflang: 'x-default', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/tools/tire-size-calculator/' }]} visual={false} eyebrow="Tires & wheels" intro="Enter the three numbers printed on a metric tire sidewall to calculate its physical dimensions and rolling distance." limitation="These are nominal geometric calculations. Real dimensions vary by tire model, rim width, pressure, load, and manufacturer tolerances." studioCta="Open Wheel & Tire Compare">
  <form slot="tool" class="calculator-form" data-calculator="tire-size" novalidate>
    <fieldset><legend>Tire size</legend><div class="tire-input-row"><label>Width<input name="widthMm" type="number" value="225" inputmode="numeric" /></label><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><label>Profile<input name="aspectRatio" type="number" value="45" inputmode="numeric" /></label><span aria-hidden="true">R</span><label>Rim<input name="rimDiameterInches" type="number" value="18" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal" /></label></div></fieldset>
    <button type="submit">Calculate tire dimensions</button><div class="inline-errors" data-errors role="alert" hidden></div><p class="result-summary is-pending" data-result-summary aria-live="polite">Your result will appear here.</p><TireSizeTechnicalVisual /><dl class="tool-results" data-results aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <div class="near-sizes" data-near-sizes hidden>
      <h3 data-near-sizes-heading></h3>
      <p class="near-sizes__note" data-near-sizes-note></p>
      <ul class="near-sizes__list" data-near-sizes-list></ul>
    </div>
  </form>
  <div slot="explanation"><TireCodeExplainer /><h2>How the geometry is calculated</h2><p>Sidewall height is width multiplied by the profile percentage. Two sidewalls plus the rim diameter, converted from inches to millimetres, gives overall diameter.</p><p>Diameter and circumference describe rolling geometry. Revolutions show the theoretical number of rotations over one mile or kilometre.</p><h2>Why the size on the sidewall actually matters</h2><p>A tire's overall diameter sets how far your car travels per wheel rotation. Fit a noticeably taller or shorter tire and your speedometer starts reading the wrong number — check the real difference with the <a href="/tools/speedometer-error-calculator/">Speedometer Error Calculator</a>. The same diameter change also shifts your effective gearing, which the <a href="/tools/gear-ratio-calculator/">Gear Ratio Calculator</a> shows directly.</p></div>
</ToolPage>
<script>import { initializeToolCalculators } from '../../../ui/tool-calculators'; import { initializeShareableToolState } from '../../../ui/shareable-tool-state'; initializeToolCalculators(); initializeShareableToolState();</script>
